{
  "about": "household channels router eval — labeled household messages routed to CHANNELS. Each household is a set of channel documents (what the channel is for, the apps bound to it with their binding descriptions, the members with speak/read) exactly as the contact gate reads them; the owner also holds every app's operator channel. `sender` is a member; the options are the channels they speak on. `ok` lists every right outcome: a channel id, `channel/app` when the channel is shared and the addressee matters, or `unclear` (asking the member is right). `dev` tunes the request design, `test` (different phrasings) is only read for the reported numbers. An app row without a description takes it from presets/<id>/preset.json (the messaging slot's reason_zh, else description_zh); the rest are defined under `apps`.",
